{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947332-cross-species-reproduction-and-sexuality","id":947332,"title":"Cross-species Reproduction and Sexuality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-09T17:06:12-07:00","id":947332,"title":"Cross-species Reproduction and Sexuality","content":"So, one the things in Werewolf is that Homid, Metis, and Lupus members belong to the same species. If Lupus Garou take human form, they can reproduce with humans without difficulty and, quite frankly, find them sexually attractive. If Homid Garou take wolf form, they can reproduce with wolves and, quite frankly, find them sexually attractive. So, how is that handled in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T17:29:30-07:00","id":947341,"title":"","content":"I'm sure this will be a productive and useful thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:21:08-07:00","id":947376,"title":"","content":"99% of the time, sex of any sort in my games is handled with a very simple phrase, &quot;Fade to Black.&quot; It's not something that gets explored at the table because it's rarely something everyone wants to play with.<br /> <br /> When this has come up, one of my go-to techniques for keeping it as mature as possible is to focus on the &quot;culture&quot; shock this sort of breeding has to deal with. In either direction that's a major conflict of instincts, learned norms, and &quot;new&quot; biological urges to overcome before it's going to work. For a lot of Garou, that's just too much work to deal with when they can breed with those born as they were, and there's all that Garou stuff to do instead of getting their groove on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:43:18-07:00","id":947385,"title":"","content":"I've played a lot of Ratkin, and breeding certainly comes up there. Like Heavy Arms said, there's always just been a fade to black or a blunt &quot;and then they had sex.&quot; I don't think many animals require much in the way of romancing... either they're in heat or not. Shifters tend to be pretty exceptional specimens, so it's really just whether the curse is going to stop them or not... and even then, there's the animal magnetism roll they can make.<br /> <br /> So all that's left to think about is the lupus-born (or whatever animal) hitting on humans. I could see that being strange and interesting roleplay, given that complicated human emotions, moral hang-ups, and strange social constructs would all be very new thoughts and concepts for a lupus to deal with when they're used to just needing to look healthy and giving a couple nudges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T00:45:05-07:00","id":947588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947332-cross-species-reproduction-and-sexuality#post947332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, one the things in Werewolf is that Homid, Metis, and Lupus members belong to the same species. If Lupus Garou take human form, they can reproduce with humans without difficulty and, quite frankly, find them sexually attractive. If Homid Garou take wolf form, they can reproduce with wolves and, quite frankly, find them sexually attractive. So, how is that handled in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>In LARP for some reason all the girls want to play a pregnant character at one time. It seems to satisfy some inner need, like playing parents with dolls. And, often enough they aim for spirits or wolves as their partners. I don't see the appeal.<br /> <br /> However, before revised stated that a child of a garou would always take the mothers breed form, we had to answer that question ourselves (yes, we LARP since before the year 2000). So, we assumed the child always takes the form of the non-shifter parent, unless it is metis. In case of spirit parentage, it is usually homid.<br /> So, a female homid garou could have a litter of wolves as babies, gain renown for that and wouldn't have to care for them that long, as they are pretty independent pretty soon, and even playable characters within 2 to 3 years, if born true (that was, if we wouldn't usually prohibit lupus characters).<br /> <br /> That said, a lupus garou would in homid form probably experience the same emotions as a human does during sex, meaning that he/she could be having sex for fun - however I think his basic instincts are against such behaviour. It would be possible to conceive however. Also, a female lupus would in homid form be fertile, even if she wasn't in lupus form (talking about mating season, not general infertility).<br /> <br /> Likewise it is probably not that much fun to conceive / have sex in lupus form for a homid garou, so there is really no reason to do so, besides wanting to have lupus children. We also rule, that while human women can conceive all year, homid garou can't do so in lupus form outside of mating season. Also male and female wolves wouldn't want intercourse outside of the wolf's natural breeding cycle. But at the right time, they could conceive a litter of wolves.<br /> Socially, only specific members of a wolf pack mate, so a homid garou coming in as an outsider to the pack has to take that place amongst the pack that is mating to get some action - or find a lone wolf to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 08-10-2016, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:15:31-07:00","id":950243,"title":"","content":"Something more productive to ask about?<br /> <br /> How much clumsyness would a Homid experience in courting a wolf, or a lupus in trying to flirt with a human of the opposite sex, especialy awkward given the curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:20:09-07:00","id":950246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/947332-cross-species-reproduction-and-sexuality?p=950243#post950243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something more productive to ask about?<br /> <br /> How much clumsyness would a Homid experience in courting a wolf, or a lupus in trying to flirt with a human of the opposite sex, especialy awkward given the curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on experience. Higher rank Garou tend to be more used to being in their alternate forms.<br /> <br /> For a homid courting a wolf, I would just look at their Primal Urge rating and take into account Animal Attraction.<br /> For lupus, the same, but with Empathy, Subterfuge,and Leadership, etc. and also take into account the Animal Attraction rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:29:36-07:00","id":950258,"title":"","content":"Animal attraction should trump species boundaries. I wonder if wolves would suffer in comparison to the attractiveness of humans. I mean, what are you going to talk about afterwards with a wolf? At least you have a chance of sharing hobbies with a human and, with human kinfolk, you have a chance at having a lifelong partner (a wolf only lives for a decade or two).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:24:03-07:00","id":950402,"title":"","content":"Was close to adding a line about animal attractioni... about how it was changed for W20, but thought better of it.<br /> <br /> Any idea Fluff wise on how the problems could arise<br /> <br /> I think it would be smoothed over a biot with kinfolk.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}